<title>USA: Chino copper labor talks resume Apr 24-25 - union.</title>
<headline>Chino copper labor talks resume Apr 24-25 - union.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stalled labor negotiations between Phelps Dodge Corp and United Steelworkers of America union representing workers at the Chino mine and production plant in New Mexico will resume April 24 and 25, a union official said.</p>
<p>Workers at Chino, which produces some 169,000 tons a year of copper, have been without a labor contract since June 30, 1996.</p>
<p>Talks have broken up without agreement several times.</p>
<p>Phelps wants to impose a pay freeze in the new labor deal but the union is resisting this.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
